            <ArticleTitle>[Development, implementation and practical use of a diagnostic score].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1078-80, 1082-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In recent years many clinical prediction rules (CPR) have been developed. Before a CPR can be used in clinical practice, different methodical steps are necessary, from the development of the score, the internal and external validation to the impact study. Before using a CPR in daily practice family doctors have to verify how the rules have been developed and whether this has been done in a population similar to the population in which they would use them. The aim of this paper is to describe the development of a CPR, and to discuss advantages and risks related to the use of CPR in order to help family doctors in their choice of scores for use in their daily practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
